{"title":"Rent — Rent — daily — today","description":"U.S. rent stands at $1,932 a month in Zillow’s September 2026 data, up 2.7% from a year earlier. This housing report explains the asking rent, then compares rental concessions: 39.6% of listings versus 37.4% last September. Rent’s share of median household income edged from 26.4% to 26.3%. Next: the $366,913 typical home value and a $1,922 monthly mortgage payment with 20% down, excluding taxes and insurance. We discuss that comparison, then show ownership’s income burden rising from 33.7% to 34.3% and the October 8 average 30-year fixed conforming mortgage rate of 7.515%. The takeaway: compare lease incentives and full ownership costs, not\n\nFor entertainment and informational purposes only. This is not financial, legal, medical, or other professional advice. Consult a qualified professional about your circumstances. We are not responsible for decisions or results based on this video.\n\n#USrentprices #averagerentinAmerica #Zillowrentreport #rentalconcessions #housingaffordability","tags":["US rent prices","average rent in America","Zillow rent report","rental concessions","housing affordability","rent vs buy","US home values","monthly mortgage payment","30 year mortgage rates","housing market 2026"],"fallback_query":"American apartment renters housing","frame":"classic","frame_color":"#ffffff","voice_id":"iP95p4xoKVk53GoZ742B","voice_gender":"male","music_mood":"light rhythmic instrumental groove, warm keys, crisp soft percussion, curious and approachable, steady moderate energy, no ominous tension, no sirens or trailer impacts","sfx":true,"voice_provider":"elevenlabs","audio_provider":"elevenlabs","reporter_on":false,"hook":"Typical U.S. asking rent is $1,932 a month in September, up 2.7% from last year.","reporter_prompt":"Five-second opening: a middle-aged American male reporter in a gray henley stands outside a real United States apartment leasing office, with apartment entrances and leasing signage clearly visible behind him. Soft daylight, warm curiosity, grounded conversational delivery. Horizontal composition with the reporter offset to leave room for an editorial overlay. Production direction for the entire video: use real American stock footage full-bleed behind every graphic. Charcoal panels, orange empha","scenes":[{"text":"Typical U.S. asking rent was $1,932 a month in September 2026, up 2.7% from a year earlier.","query":"apartment leasing office American","subject":"apartment leasing office","visual":{"type":"broadcast","headline":"APARTMENT LEASING OFFICE","value":"$1,932","color":"dark","sub":"a month · Typical U.S."},"clip":{"url":"https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2026/01/15/327916_large.mp4","kind":"video","author":"StuieStu (Pixabay)"},"clips":[{"url":"https://cdn.pixabay.com/video/2026/01/15/327916_large.mp4","kind":"video","author":"StuieStu (Pixabay)"},{"url":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1770938474431-d1192cac9642?ixid=M3wxMDkyNjk3fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MjN8fFN1YnVyYmFuJTIwaG9tZXN8ZW58MXx8fHwxNzkxMzQwMjEwfDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=2400&fit=max&q=85","kind":"photo","author":"Daniel Miksha (Unsplash)"}],"presentationOnly":false},{"text":"Rental concessions can lower your overall lease cost, even when the advertised monthly rent is higher.","query":"renter American apartment bills","subject":"renter","visual":{"type":"title","headline":"RENTER","color":"dark"},"clip":{"url":"https://pixabay.com/get/g5236613513d517ff76ebc6c2442e15c457bed74cd18acbb608d8694ba05fff8268a15dff00cac3cfb979fc239a7e81254f90cd7bff4e3af4108581c44ef96dc6_1280.jpg","kind":"photo","author":"atanaspaskalev (Pixabay)"},"clips":[{"url":"https://pixabay.com/get/g5236613513d517ff76ebc6c2442e15c457bed74cd18acbb608d8694ba05fff8268a15dff00cac3cfb979fc239a7e81254f90cd7bff4e3af4108581c44ef96dc6_1280.jpg","kind":"photo","author":"atanaspaskalev (Pixabay)"},{"url":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1560448204-e02f11c3d0e2?ixid=M3wxMDkyNjk3fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8Nnx8cmVhbCUyMGVzdGF0ZXxlbnwxfHx8fDE3OTEzMDk4Mjh8M